# A low-pass filter: a square wave through a resistor into a capacitor.
#
# The capacitor cannot follow the square wave's sudden steps. It charges a little while the input is
# high and discharges a little while it is low, so the output is the input's average, 2.5 V, with a
# small ripple left on it. A larger resistor or capacitor smooths it more.

speed 2m

source    V1  0 0  0 6  square 0 5 1k
resistor  R1  0 0  6 0  1k
capacitor C1  6 0  6 6  2.2u
wire          6 6  0 6
ground        0 6
meter     IN  0 0  0 6
meter     OUT 6 0  6 6
